{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Construct sweep from 7dea/d284: shared deterministic .tmp + os.replace across concurrent writers\n\nThe shared-deterministic-temp collision class proven in 7dea (completion_verdict_cache, Gerrit 2329) and d284 (plan_review/sizing.save_checkpoint, Gerrit 2334): a site composes a temp name deterministically from the target (tmp = f\"{self.path}.tmp\", NOT unique-per-writer), writes it, then os.replace(tmp, final). Under two concurrent writers for the same target the first os.replace consumes the shared temp and the second raises FileNotFoundError, which the site swallows (log+return) -> the losing writer silently loses its own write.\n\n## Sweep outcome -- 2 CONFIRMED live siblings; others analyzed and excluded (see RCA comment)\n\nConfirmed siblings (both in rebar_reconciler; the ONLY two of the package's seven atomic-write sites not already using unique-per-writer tempfile.mkstemp):\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/peer_confirmations.py -- PeerConfirmationStore.save().\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/impossible_links.py -- ImpossibleLinkStore.save().\n\nConcurrency: both write the per-repo committed .bridge_state/*.json sidecar; passes serialize on refs/reconciler/lock but the lease is steal-able and there is NO lock-lost guard before the persistence-phase save(), so the zombie/lease-steal window admits two concurrent writers. Fix: unique-per-writer tempfile.mkstemp + atomic replace onto the shared final (last-write-wins preserved); on failure unlink only the writer's own temp then log-and-return (fail-open contract PRESERVED -- these best-effort stores must never raise into a pass).\n\nExcluded (documented in RCA comment): review_bot/reconcile._write_cursor (single sequential reconcile_loop task, single-box PoC), _config_writer/_cli config writes (one-shot), _opcert_signing (PID-unique + byte-identical .pub content -> no data loss), and all mkstemp/fsutil/write-lock sites.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] peer_confirmations.py::PeerConfirmationStore.save() uses a unique-per-writer temp (tempfile.mkstemp), with a RED-first regression proving two concurrent same-target save() writers both persist (both _dirty cleared) and leave no .tmp residue.\n- [ ] impossible_links.py::ImpossibleLinkStore.save() uses a unique-per-writer temp (tempfile.mkstemp), with a RED-first regression proving two concurrent same-target save() writers both persist and leave no .tmp residue.\n- [ ] Structural class check: the regression suite fails if either save() reverts to a deterministic shared <path>.tmp (mutation-checked -- re-introducing the shared name returns the test to RED).\n- [ ] Fail-open behavior preserved: a save() write error is swallowed (logged), never raised into the reconciler pass (existing AC8 fail-open tests still pass).\n- [ ] Excluded candidates each have a documented concurrency verdict with evidence (RCA comment)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787950999501810001,"uuid":"f6971898-2aac-4de6-9349-6134f5942828"}